// src/tool_ident.pdx — mkdir v1.2.0
//
// ToolIdent module: per-tool identity extern consumed by
// libpdx-argv >= 1.1.3 VersionBackend::emit_default (ENH-032 hotfix,
// paideia-os/libpdx-argv #42).
//
// Why this file exists — Wave 6 libpdx-argv contract
// --------------------------------------------------
// libpdx-argv 1.1.3 removed the hard-coded `DOC_TOOL_NAME` /
// `DOC_TOOL_VERSION` literals from VersionBackend::emit_default and
// replaced them with two `UND` externs — PDX_TOOL_NAME (lowercase,
// NUL-terminated) and PDX_TOOL_VERSION (semver, NUL-terminated).
// Every consumer of libpdx-argv >= 1.1.3 must provide both symbols
// at final-link time or `ld` fails with an undefined-symbol error
// naming the missing symbol (deliberate: no STB_WEAK fallback
// because the pre-hotfix "doc" default would silently pass under
// `--version` — worse than a link-time failure).
//
// See tools/user/libpdx-argv/src/version_backend.pdx §60-90 for
// the full contract and the ENH-032 hotfix rationale.
//
// Wire-in posture at v1.2.0
// -------------------------
// mkdir's satellite deps.list does NOT declare libpdx-argv at v1.2.0
// — the tool inlines its three syscalls (sys_debug_puts, sys_exit,
// sys_mkdir) plus the R86 sys_getcwd and R107 sys_semantic_send
// additions, and reads argv directly from the frozen execve ABI
// (rdi=argc, rsi=argv). PDX_TOOL_NAME is declared here PROVISIONALLY
// (matching cat/src/tool_ident.pdx v1.2.0-A posture) so a future
// v1.3 landing that adds a Parser::parse_argv call — the natural
// substrate for `-m <mode>` and `-p` at that milestone — links
// against libpdx-argv without a fresh caps.decl edit and without a
// deps.list churn on the tool-ident symbol.
//
// PDX_TOOL_VERSION is intentionally OMITTED at v1.2.0. Two reasons:
//
//   (a) libpdx-argv's emit_default requires BOTH symbols; a partial
//       declaration is worse than none (the tool would half-satisfy
//       the extern and produce a name/version mismatch under a
//       future --version implementation). Adding PDX_TOOL_VERSION
//       here without a `--version` code path invites a doc-truth
//       drift between this literal and the CHANGELOG's tag —
//       exactly the ENH-032 regression class the hotfix was cutting.
//
//   (b) mkdir has no `--version` implementation today (v1.1-A
//       explicitly retired the --version flag when it retired the
//       whole flag parser). Adding PDX_TOOL_VERSION as a symbol
//       without a consumer creates an unused-symbol footprint and
//       an unnecessary two-line update on every version bump.
//
// The v1.3 landing that adds `-m` / `-p` (and re-adds --version
// as an emit_default entry point) adds PDX_TOOL_VERSION here.
//
// paideia-as compliance
// ---------------------
//   - Module name PascalCase basename (`ToolIdent`).
//   - No function bodies -> no register plan, no push/pop parity,
//     no encoder guardrails to enforce here.
//   - String literal on a single line (fingerprint-extractor
//     requirement + libpdx-argv linker resolves the symbol as-is).
//   - Array size == literal byte count including NUL: "mkdir\0" = 6
//     bytes.
//   - `pub let` (public + immutable = .rodata) so a future
//     libpdx-argv link can resolve the UND ref against it.

module ToolIdent = structure {

  // ============================================================================
  // PDX_TOOL_NAME — lowercase tool name, NUL-terminated. Read by
  // libpdx-argv VersionBackend::emit_default at run time via the
  // `lea rdi, [rip + PDX_TOOL_NAME]` idiom (segment 1a of the
  // ENH-032 emit_default body); the byte-count is computed via
  // VersionBackend::version_strlen and clamped to
  // TOOL_NAME_UPPER_MAX (32 bytes) for the uppercase mirror.
  // "mkdir" fits trivially; the array is 6 bytes including NUL.
  // ============================================================================
  pub let PDX_TOOL_NAME : [u8; 6] = "mkdir\0"

}
